From 44b8c66faea273d2426c3a16d7c1b6b7a6540195 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ccchang <willychang17@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:41:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Perf] systemone: Validate decision layouts without importing
 the joint schema head

The tokenizer manager and the /v1/systemone entrypoints only pack, parse
and bound decision layouts, which is plain Python. They imported it from
layers/joint_schema_head.py, whose pooler import reaches the quantization
registry, linear, MoE and DeepGEMM runners and torch._inductor.

Move QUESTION_TYPES, LayoutQuestion, max_joint_prompt_tokens and
pack/parse_decision_layout to layers/joint_schema_layout.py (no torch)
and import them from there. The head imports them back; behavior is
unchanged. Add a fresh-interpreter test that the layout module does not
load torch and the systemone frontend does not load the head or the
quantization registry.

Refs #10492
